//! task: fix
//! ask: Return a true value from a function.
//! expect: EXS-E0301
//! refs: §8.4
//! explain: Exsecutor has no `true` or `false`: they are not keywords and nothing predefines them, so `true` is an unresolved name, `EXS-E0301`. A truth value is the one-bit type `u1`, written 1 and 0. Conditions are written with the comparison words, `si x gt 0 { ... }`, and are not values of a boolean type.

publica functio f() -> u1 {
    redde true;
}
//@ fixed
publica functio f() -> u1 {
    redde 1;
}
